[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Najdorf"]
[Variation "Sicilian Defense: Najdorf Variation"]
[ECO "B96"]
[Character "sharp,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "queenside-expansion,solid-centre"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6
6. Bg5 e6 { Builds a solid centre and lets the f8 bishop out. Black can then answer the bishop on g5 with ...Be7 and ...Nbd7. }
7. f4 (7. Bxf6 Qxf6 { Black keeps the two bishops, which is a long-term plus. } 8. Qd2 Nc6 { Challenges the knight on d4, White's most active piece. })
7... Be7 { Unpins the knight on f6 and gets ready to castle. }
8. Qf3 (8. Bxf6 Bxf6 { The bishop recaptures and eyes the knight on d4. } 9. Qd2 Nc6 { Black asks the knight to move.})
8... Qc7 { Eyes the c-file, where White's king is likely to castle, and protects the d6 pawn. }
9. O-O-O
9... Nbd7 { Brings out the last minor piece and prepares ...b5 and ...Nc5. }
10. Bd3 (10. g4 b5 { Starts a pawn attack on the queenside, where White's king is heading, before White's own g-pawn push gets going. } 11. Bxf6 Nxf6 { Recaptures with the knight, which stays in touch with e4 and g4. } 12. g5 Nd7 { The knight retreats to a safe square, from where it supports ...Ne5 or ...Nc5. })
10... b5 { Gains queenside space and prepares ...Bb7, which lines up against the e4 pawn. }
11. Rhe1 Bb7 *
